.TH FEEDOPUS 1 "October 2026" "feedopus" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
feedopus \- save new videos from selected feeds as Opus audio
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B feedopus
.RI [ run-option ]...
.br
.B feedopus run
.RI [ option ]...
.br
.B feedopus grab
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-output\-dir
.IR dir ]
.I url
.br
.B feedopus init
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.br
.B feedopus list
.br
.B feedopus status
.br
.B feedopus install\-timer
.br
.B feedopus remove\-timer
.br
.B feedopus install\-docs
.br
.B feedopus self\-test
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B feedopus
reads the feeds you select and saves new uploads as Opus audio.
Livestreams, upcoming streams, and archived livestreams (stream VODs) are skipped.
The video thumbnail is embedded as cover art inside the Opus file.
Finished files go to
.I ~/Sync/podcast
unless
.B output_dir
points somewhere else.
Partial downloads stay in the state directory, so Syncthing does not sync a half-written file.
.PP
With no command,
.B feedopus
does what
.B run
does.
A first argument that starts with a dash is also passed to
.BR run ,
except
.B \-h
and
.BR \-\-help .
.PP
It runs on Linux.
It needs Python 3.11 or newer, yt-dlp, and ffmpeg with libopus.
.B feedopus
is free software under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Check the feed list and download new audio. This is the default command.
.TP
.BI grab " url"
Save one video URL as audio. The URL is also checked against audio already in the output folder.
.TP
.B init
Write
.I ~/.config/feedopus/config
and
.IR ~/.config/feedopus/feeds .
Video feeds found in newsboat's URL file are copied in. Blogs and distro news are left out.
.B \-\-force
overwrites both files.
.TP
.B list
Print the selected feeds.
.TP
.B status
Print how many items are remembered, grouped as downloaded, skipped, seen, deferred, and error.
.TP
.B clean
Delete the oldest audio files in the output folder.
The newest
.B keep_episodes
files stay (default 30).
.B \-\-keep N
uses N for this run.
.B \-\-dry\-run
lists the files that would be deleted and removes nothing.
A removed file stays remembered, so it is not downloaded again.
.TP
.B install\-timer
Write and enable a systemd user timer that runs about every two hours, at :20 past even hours.
It does not start the timer.
Start it with
.BR "systemctl \-\-user start feedopus.timer" .
.TP
.B remove\-timer
Disable that timer and delete its unit files.
.TP
.B install\-docs
Install this manual and the tldr page for the current user.
.TP
.B self\-test
Run offline checks. Nothing is downloaded.
.SH OPTIONS
Options for
.B run
can be given with or without the
.B run
word.
.B grab
accepts
.BR \-\-dry\-run ,
.BR \-\-output\-dir ,
.BR \-\-config\-dir ,
and
.BR \-\-state\-dir .
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Decide what would be saved. Files and state are left unchanged.
.TP
.BI \-\-since\-days " N"
Only consider items newer than
.I N
days.
The first time a feed is read, this window comes from the
.B since_days
setting (default 2), and older items are marked seen.
On later runs, new items are downloaded at any age.
Passing this option applies the window on those later runs as well.
.TP
.BI \-\-backfill " N"
From each feed, take the
.I N
newest items that are not already saved, and mark the rest seen.
.TP
.BI \-\-max " N"
Stop after
.I N
download attempts. The default is the
.B max_per_run
setting (8).
Items skipped because they are still live do not count toward this limit.
.TP
.B \-\-retry
Try items that have already failed three times.
.TP
.BI \-\-output\-dir " dir"
Write finished audio here for this run, instead of the
.B output_dir
setting.
.TP
.BI \-\-config\-dir " dir"
Directory that holds
.I config
and the feed list.
The default is
.IR ~/.config/feedopus ,
or
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/feedopus
when that variable is set.
.TP
.BI \-\-state\-dir " dir"
Directory for the seen-item database, the yt-dlp archive, the log, and partial downloads.
The default is
.IR ~/.local/state/feedopus ,
or
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/feedopus
when that variable is set.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short reminder of the commands.
.B "feedopus run \-\-help"
shows the options for a run.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/feedopus/config
Settings, one
.B key = value
per line.
A line that starts with # is a comment.
A ~ in a path is expanded.
Percent signs are kept as written, which is what the filename template needs.
.TP
.I ~/.config/feedopus/feeds
One URL per line, in newsboat style:
.RS
.EX
https://www.youtube.com/feeds/videos.xml?channel_id=UCxxxx "Channel name"
https://www.youtube.com/@Channel "Channel name"
.EE
.RE
.IP
An optional tag may follow the name.
A YouTube address of the form
.I feeds/videos.xml?channel_id=UCxxxx
is read as RSS.
If that request fails, the channel's uploads playlist is checked instead,
the same id with
.B UC
changed to
.BR UU .
A
.I playlist_id
on that host is read as that playlist when RSS fails.
Other RSS and Atom URLs are read directly.
Any other URL is treated as a channel or playlist, and only the newest
.B playlist_end
entries are considered (default 15).
.TP
.I ~/Sync/podcast
Finished audio, unless
.B output_dir
says otherwise.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/feedopus/state.json
Items already considered, and which feeds have been caught up.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/feedopus/archive.txt
yt-dlp download archive.
A listed video whose audio file is no longer in the output folder is downloaded again.
That case is not reported as an error.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/feedopus/tmp
Partial downloads and thumbnail files. Old partials are removed after 7 days.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/feedopus/feedopus.log
Log of recent runs.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/feedopus.timer
User timer written by
.BR install\-timer ,
together with
.IR feedopus.service .
The timer runs
.B feedopus run
about every two hours.
.SH CONFIGURATION
These keys live in the config file. The values below are the defaults.
.TP
.B output_dir
Directory for finished files.
Default:
.IR ~/Sync/podcast .
.TP
.B filename
yt-dlp output template, relative to the output directory.
Default:
.EX
%(title)s.%(ext)s
.EE
The finished file is renamed to the title alone, with spaces and punctuation
written as underscores and emoji removed, so it matches a Grayjay download.
A period at the end of the title is dropped, so the extension is the only dot.
.TP
.B audio_format
Container written by yt-dlp.
Default:
.IR opus .
.TP
.B audio_quality
Passed through to yt-dlp.
Default:
.I 0
(best).
.TP
.B embed_thumbnail
Embed the video thumbnail as JPEG cover art, the same kind of picture Grayjay stores.
Default:
.IR true .
The audio is copied, not re-encoded.
If the thumbnail cannot be fetched, the audio is still kept and the log says that cover art was not embedded.
.TP
.B sponsorblock
SponsorBlock categories to cut, separated by commas.
Default:
.IR sponsor,selfpromo,interaction .
An empty value keeps the whole recording.
.TP
.B since_days
Age window used the first time a feed is read.
Default:
.IR 2 .
.TP
.B max_per_run
Maximum downloads in one run.
Default:
.IR 8 .
.TP
.B skip_live
Skip videos that are live or scheduled to go live.
Default:
.IR true .
Those items are checked again on a later run.
.TP
.B skip_was_live
Skip the saved recording of a livestream.
Default:
.IR true .
A normal video that YouTube premiered is sometimes labeled as a past livestream, and is then skipped while this is true.
.TP
.B live_give_up_days
Stop rechecking a livestream after this many days.
Default:
.IR 14 .
.TP
.B playlist_end
How many recent videos to read from a channel or playlist URL.
Default:
.IR 15 .
.TP
.B sleep_seconds
Pause between yt-dlp calls.
Default:
.IR 1 .
.TP
.B download_timeout_minutes
Give up on one download after this many minutes.
Default:
.IR 45 .
.TP
.B cookies
Path of a Netscape cookies file, for age-restricted videos.
Empty means no cookies file.
.TP
.B extra_args
Extra arguments appended to every yt-dlp download, written in shell syntax.
Empty by default.
.TP
.B notify
Send a notification when a run saves files or hits errors.
Uses notify-send.
Default:
.IR true .
.TP
.B windows_filenames
Ask yt-dlp to avoid characters that phone storage rejects.
Default:
.IR true .
.TP
.B feeds_file
Path of the feed list.
The default is
.I feeds
inside the config directory.
.TP
.B require_tag
When set, only feed lines that carry this tag are used.
Empty uses every line.
.TP
.B keep_episodes
How many of the newest audio files
.B clean
leaves in the output folder.
Default:
.IR 30 .
Older audio files are the ones removed.
.B 0
removes every audio file in that folder.
.SH "FIRST VISIT"
The first time a feed is read, only items newer than
.B since_days
are candidates.
Older items, and items with no date, are marked seen and left alone.
Later runs download anything in the feed that has not been seen.
A feed that could not be fetched is not treated as caught up, so the next run tries the first-visit window again.
.PP
.B "run \-\-backfill N"
takes the
.I N
newest unsaved items from each feed and marks the rest seen.
Those selected items are still saved from oldest to newest.
.SH ORDER
Each channel is saved from oldest to newest.
Channels take turns, following the order of the feed list, so the first channel does not use every download slot in the run.
An entry with no date is saved after the dated ones from that channel.
.SH DUPLICATES
A title that matches audio already in the output folder is skipped, including a Grayjay download whose name lost its emoji and punctuation or was cut short.
Letters and digits are compared, and apostrophes are ignored, so a title like "I'm" matches a file named with "I_m" or "Im".
A title that only adds a number, such as "Title 2", is still downloaded.
The same upload seen on YouTube and again on Odysee is saved once.
Two different videos that share a long opening can be treated as the same file.
.PP
Run
.B feedopus
on one device at a time.
Two devices that have not synced the finished file yet can each download a copy.
.SH INSTALL
On Linux, from a copy of the project directory:
.EX
\&./install\-linux
.EE
This copies the program to
.IR ~/.local/bin/feedopus ,
replacing any older file or symlink there.
It installs Python 3.11 or newer, ffmpeg with libopus, and yt-dlp when they are missing,
writes a config if this user has none, replaces this manual and the tldr page, and enables the timer.
It does not start the timer.
.B \-\-start
starts it.
.B \-\-state\-from
.I dir
copies
.I state.json
and
.I archive.txt
from
.I dir
when this user does not already have those files.
An existing config and feed list are kept.
If
.B feeds_file
names a path that is not on this machine, it is pointed at
.I ~/.config/feedopus/feeds
when that file exists.
.B install\-docs
installs the manual and the tldr page when those viewers are available.
The manual, the tldr page, and
.I fish/tldr.fish
have to sit next to the program file for that command to find them.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
feedopus
feedopus run \-\-dry\-run
feedopus run \-\-backfill 3
feedopus run \-\-since\-days 7 \-\-max 2
feedopus grab 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VIDEO_ID'
feedopus init
feedopus list
feedopus status
feedopus clean \-\-dry\-run
feedopus clean \-\-keep 30
feedopus install\-timer
systemctl \-\-user start feedopus.timer
feedopus install\-docs
.EE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR yt\-dlp (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR newsboat (1)
